This repo is Anoop's ECE 210 project H02 (UC Santa Cruz): train a differentiable
logic-gate network (Petersen et al., NeurIPS 2022), discretize it, export Verilog,
verify RTL bit-exact against the Python golden model, and measure FPGA resources,
timing and switching power. His extension is power-aware training: penalize
2p(1-p) per gate, with p the batch-mean soft output, and plot accuracy vs. measured energy.
It is planned to grow into his master's project and a paper.

Full background, dates, open decisions and status: @docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md

How to help:
- He is learning this deeply. Explain one small piece at a time, in plain language,
  with a concrete example (cover What, How, Where, Why, When).
- Wait for him to say "yes, understood" before moving to the next piece.
- Say what a command will do before running anything long or heavy.
- When changing code, explain the change so he understands it, not just the result.
- `dlgn/hard.py` is the golden model; RTL must match it bit for bit (argmax ties -> lowest index).
- Key dates: proposal Oct 30, 2026; final Dec 4, 2026.
